The data behind decision record 0042, the chrome is drawn from a theme.

The Rust fixture tests in crates/domux-core/src/theme are the reference: fixture.rs holds the
same 22 answers, and the tests in guard.rs pin the values these files produced. The files here
record where those values came from. Nothing in the build or the test suite reads them.

omarchy-themes.json
    The 22 themes Omarchy ships, as of 2026-09-13: each theme's background, foreground and
    palette slots 0 to 15, which a Ghostty drawing that theme answers at attach. They were
    rendered from /usr/share/omarchy/themes/<name>/colors.toml through Omarchy's Ghostty
    template. Each theme also carries its mode, accent, cursor and selection colours and a few
    figures derived from the rest.

lib.py
    The colour arithmetic the models share: WCAG contrast, OKLCH, and the loaded json.

terminal_theme3.py
    The model of the terminal theme with the guards for grounds, text tiers and colours, and
    the hue test.

terminal_theme4.py
    The model the record's numbers came from. It extends terminal_theme3.py with the floors for
    the kind colours, the band ends, the lines and the stay awake dot for "not held".

Run it with Python 3 from any directory:

    python3 docs/decisions/0042-data/terminal_theme4.py all
        One line per theme: ok when every guard holds, and what moved.
    python3 docs/decisions/0042-data/terminal_theme4.py five [theme ...]
        The value and contrast of every role on the five themes the brief named.
    python3 docs/decisions/0042-data/terminal_theme4.py summary
        The lines, kinds and band ends moved on all 22 themes.
